rs claims return as new group Inception denies links</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/shinyhunters-claims-return-as-new-group-inception-denies-links/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/shinyhunters-claims-return-as-new-group-inception-denies-links/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:20:37 +0000</pubDate><description>A message on a cybercrime forum claims the notorious ShinyHunters group is back, while a new group called Inception denies any connection.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/370/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"><media:credit role="illustrator">AI-generated illustration</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>Independent review launched into UK data watchdog culture</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/independent-review-launched-into-uk-data-watchdog-culture/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/independent-review-launched-into-uk-data-watchdog-culture/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:20:18 +0000</pubDate><description>An independent review has been appointed to investigate claims of a toxic workplace culture at the Information Commissioner&#x27;s Office.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/369/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"><media:credit role="illustrator">AI-generated illustration</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>Fake snipping tool app used to install spyware</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/fake-snipping-tool-app-used-to-install-spyware/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/fake-snipping-tool-app-used-to-install-spyware/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:19:45 +0000</pubDate><description>Researchers found a fake app in the Microsoft Store that installs spyware, so you should check your downloads.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/368/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"></media:content></item><item><title>Medical firm Boston Scientific confirms data breach</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/medical-firm-boston-scientific-confirms-data-breach/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/medical-firm-boston-scientific-confirms-data-breach/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:19:08 +0000</pubDate><description>A cyberattack exposed the personal and medical details of 117,789 people, prompting the company to send out warning letters.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/367/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"><media:credit role="illustrator">AI-generated illustration</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>pCloud confirms password manager hack after suspicious login alerts</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/pcloud-confirms-password-manager-hack-after-suspicious-login-alerts/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/pcloud-confirms-password-manager-hack-after-suspicious-login-alerts/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:17:33 +0000</pubDate><description>pCloud has confirmed a cyberattack on its password manager.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/366/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"></media:content></item><item><title>Telegram warns iPhone users to update software</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/telegram-warns-iphone-users-to-update-software/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/28/telegram-warns-iphone-users-to-update-software/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:16:50 +0000</pubDate><description>Telegram says iPhone users with older software are being hacked just by visiting websites, so you should check for updates now.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/365/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"><media:credit role="illustrator">AI-generated illustration</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>Old ShinyHunters account posts on leak site</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/old-shinyhunters-account-posts-on-leak-site/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/old-shinyhunters-account-posts-on-leak-site/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:00:24 +0000</pubDate><description>A post signed with an old key suggests the ShinyHunters group may be active again, but the signature does not prove the post is genuine.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/342/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"><media:credit role="illustrator">AI-generated illustration</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>Dell fixes critical flaw in network switch software</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/dell-fixes-critical-flaw-in-network-switch-software/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/dell-fixes-critical-flaw-in-network-switch-software/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:00:22 +0000</pubDate><description>Dell has released a fix for a serious security weakness in its Enterprise SONiC software that could allow attackers to run commands on network switches.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/341/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"></media:content></item><item><title>Old passwords often stay active for years, report finds</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/old-passwords-often-stay-active-for-years-report-finds/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/old-passwords-often-stay-active-for-years-report-finds/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:00:08 +0000</pubDate><description>A new report shows that most old digital keys found in 2022 still worked in 2026, highlighting a slow process for removing them.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/340/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"><media:credit role="illustrator">AI-generated illustration</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>Hackers use AI tools to speed up network attacks</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/hackers-use-ai-tools-to-speed-up-network-attacks/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/hackers-use-ai-tools-to-speed-up-network-attacks/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:59:48 +0000</pubDate><description>Researchers found that AI agents helped criminals move faster through company systems, but the speed also makes the activity easier to spot.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/339/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"><media:credit role="illustrator">AI-generated illustration</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>AI hacking tools are being used more often, say researchers</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/ai-hacking-tools-are-being-used-more-often-say-researchers/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.gi