ded smart boilers connect to servers in Russia, raising privacy concerns for household data.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/301/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"></media:content></item><item><title>Home Office reprimanded over border data errors</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/home-office-reprimanded-over-border-data-errors/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/home-office-reprimanded-over-border-data-errors/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:20:10 +0000</pubDate><description>The UK data protection regulator has reprimanded the Home Office for failing to keep border control records accurate, which led to some people being wrongly detained.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/300/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"><media:credit role="illustrator">AI-generated illustration</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>Fake login pages built with AI found on Hugging Face</title><link>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/fake-login-pages-built-with-ai-found-on-hugging-face/</link><guid>https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/2026/11/27/fake-login-pages-built-with-ai-found-on-hugging-face/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:17:55 +0000</pubDate><description>Criminals used an AI tool to create fake websites that looked like Microsoft and PayPal, tricking people into giving up their passwords.</description><media:content url="https://theknowledgecabinet.github.io/stay-safe-online/assets/media/299/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"></media:content></item></channel></rss>
